lazine, Infliximab continued</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Case 2</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">46/M</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">AS</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Psoriasis</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5 months</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Resolution after switching to etanercept</td></tr><tr><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Case 3</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">46/F</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Psoriasis</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Arthritis</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">7 months</td><td align="center" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Resolution after switching to etanercept </td></tr></tbody></table></table-wrap><table-wrap id="T2" position="float"><label>Table 2</label><caption><p>Clinical and Demographic Charasteristics of Patients Who Developed Psoriasis Under Treatment with TNF &#x003b1; Blocker</p></caption><table frame="border" rules="all" width="100%"><tbody><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Gender</bold></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">57 Females, 33 Males, 3 UK</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Mean Age; Range</bold></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">45;13-78</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Underlying disease</bold></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">44 RA, 2 JRA,9 Crohn, 1 UC, <break/>17 AS (+4 Crohn), 2 Behcet, <break/>1 PsA,1 eosinophilic fasceitis, 1 uveitis </td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Concomitant drugs</bold></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">None 6, Methotrexate 22 Prednisone 8, Salazopyrine 5, Leflunomide 8, <break/> Azathioprine 3</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Infliximab</bold></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">47</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Etanercept</bold></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1">17</td></tr><tr><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"><bold>Adalimumab</bold></td><td rowspan="1" colspan="1"